Prefers comprehensive documentation and tracking.
Plan file: keep ONE consolidated file. `.lovable/plan.md` = Lovable-internal active roadmap; `/plan.md` = public handoff for other AIs. Both stay in sync.
Suggestions: ONE FILE PER SUGGESTION under `.lovable/memory/suggestions/NN-slug.md` (per `.lovable/memory/suggestions/README.md`). The legacy `.lovable/suggestions.md` is now an index pointer only.
Pending issues: one file per issue under `.lovable/pending-issues/NN-slug.md`; resolved ones move to `.lovable/solved-issues/`.
Strictly-avoid: keep ONE consolidated `.lovable/strictly-avoid.md`.
Uses Malaysia timezone (UTC+8).
Expects readme.txt milestone markers with format: "let's start now {date} {time}".
Wants reliability reports before implementation.
Plans to hand off specs to other AI models — needs clear, self-contained docs.
File naming: 01-name-of-file.md numbered prefix convention.
Never touch .release folder. Code changes must bump at least minor version.
Do NOT append the "If you have any question and confusion..." boilerplate block.
Do NOT append the "Do you understand? Always add this part..." code block.
Always list remaining tasks at the end of each completed work session. If all tasks are done, find remaining items from memory and suggest next actions.
